  "correctness_review": {
    "workspace_pool": "The thread-local LRU retains at most 1 GiB and 64 slots per caller thread. Acquisition removes the newest exact-size match; release evicts oldest slots until both bounds fit, frees oversize buffers immediately, and the thread-local destructor frees remaining slots. Current GEMM buffers are owned and destroyed by the calling thread; packed storage is only shared by reference through the completed OpenMP region. No correctness issue found.",
    "permission_and_dispatch": "The cached PID mismatch after fork forces an inherited-permission recheck; concurrent first requests are safe under process-wide kernel permission semantics. A fresh-process 64-thread simultaneous request test succeeded 64/64, and a fork child observed inherited permission. Generic dispatch checks CPU features and OS XSTATE before calling the target-specific implementation. No correctness issue found."
  },
